  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting material is a uniform, fine-lamellar AlCoCrFeNi2.1 eutectic high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting AlCoCrFeNi2.1 alloy has insufficient strength and plasticity for industrial fastener applications.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add approximately 2 at.% Nb during alloy synthesis.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Nb will induce an Nb-rich secondary phase in AlCoCrFeNi2.1.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-rich secondary phase will be fine, coherent, and finely dispersed within an FCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A small Nb addition can form a new Laves secondary phase in a CoCrFeNi matrix.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hard secondary phases produced by minor Nb, Ti, or Mo additions can precipitation-strengthen CoCrFeNi and improve its mechanical properties.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-rich precipitates will impede dislocation motion through precipitation strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-rich precipitates will locally increase elastic modulus.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb addition will increase the yield strength of AlCoCrFeNi2.1.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7287792::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb addition will decrease creep rate and improve creep resistance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The strength and creep improvements will occur without sacrificing ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-modified alloy will retain comparable or improved corrosion resistance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb will form stable surface oxides that improve corrosion resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Operation and testing are proposed from ambient temperature to approximately 500°C or the onset of phase instability.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Corrosion performance is to be evaluated in 3.5 wt.% NaCl solution.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline and Nb-modified samples will receive identical thermomechanical processing and be compared using tensile, creep, corrosion, thermal-cycling, and microstructural tests.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
